    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38230" root="مجد" body-key="m">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاجِدٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجِيدٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, applied to a
camel: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجَدَتِ الإِبِلُ</span>: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجَّدٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجُدٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَاجِدُ</span>. (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاجِدٌ</span> <i>Much; abundant;</i>
syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَثِيرٌ</span>. (K, TA.) [In the CK, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَثِيرٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَجْدِ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَيْسَتْ بِمَاجِدَةٍ لِلطَّعَامِ وَلَا لِلشَّرَابِ</span> <i>She
does not eat</i> or <i>drink much.</i> Said by Aboo-
Habbeh, describing a woman. (L.)

